&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;投票并不能帮到作者。但讨论和批评可以。我在此立誓我将给我差评的每篇文章留下评论（但愿大部分我好评的文章也是如此）。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;我的理论在此：&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;a class=&quot;newpage&quot; href=&quot;http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/abolish-the-no-vote-downvote-your-friends-and-other-scp-crit&quot;&gt;Abolish The No Vote, Downvote Your Friends, and Other Musings&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1229263&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1607519879&quot; alt=&quot;RJB_R&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1229263)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r&quot;  &gt;RJB_R&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;若你也同意，请在评分后留下讨论和批评来帮助作者。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;你能在这一页的底部找到一系列我为什么可能不喜欢你的作品的理由。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;如果你读过我的一篇文章，感觉有什么话要说，请留下评论！正面的、负面的或者两者之间的，我很乐意知道我的写作让你感觉到/想到了什么。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span&gt;CSS主题&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;定制的主题，用以给任何页面泼上视觉风格。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span&gt;版式&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;模块化工具，用以为文章添加功能。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;我投差评的常见原因&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;我的规则是：只要在你的页面源代码里，我就能据此投票。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;一般来说我没有看到就差评的东西，但有很多东西会让我以负面的态度看待你写的文章。这些是描述我个人观点的指南——它们并不是硬道理，而且它们&lt;strong&gt;绝对&lt;/strong&gt;不&lt;em&gt;决定&lt;/em&gt;我的观点。I don&#039;t really have any instant-downvote triggers, but there&#039;s a bunch of things that&#039;ll make me see your article in a negative light. These are guidelines that describe my opinions - they are not hard rules, and they &lt;strong&gt;definitely&lt;/strong&gt; do not &lt;em&gt;define&lt;/em&gt; my opinions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;给大多数文章的指南&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;难看/偷懒的格式：Poor/lazy formatting:&lt;/strong&gt;这个可能适用于网站上70%的文章，但如果你的文章只是一页文字的话，我就会先入为主地产生负面印象。如果你不能花时间让你的页面看起来在视觉上有趣一点，我又为什么要花时间去看呢？一张图是一个很好的打破单调的方式，可以让我在看之前就被吸引。 This probably applies to a good 70% of articles on the site, but if your article is just a page of text, I&#039;m already looking at it in a negative light. If you couldn&#039;t take the time to make your page visually interesting, why should I take the time to read it? An image is a great way to break the monotony and get me invested without even having to make me read anything.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;警告：Caveat:&lt;/strong&gt;你的格式需要和你的内容相匹配。一篇短的、简单的文章需要简单的格式。一篇长的、更详细的文章可以在“我就想这么弄”的格式上宽容一点。不要戴高礼帽穿T恤。 Your formatting should match the content. A short, simple article should have simple formatting. A longer, more elaborate article can get away with a bit more &#039;just because I want to&#039; formatting. Don&#039;t wear a top hat and a t-shirt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;排除别人：Excluding people:&lt;/strong&gt;这个网站的主要构成人员是美国人，所以如果一篇文章直接假设我就住在美国，而我其实住在英国，我就会感觉被排挤了。比如说，如果你说“SCP-XXXX位于北卡罗来纳”而没有点明“美国北卡罗来纳”，你在预设看这篇SCP文档的人在美国，引申开来整个基金会也就在美国，所以作为英国读者，我就没有被算在里面了。请确保你的地点是国际化的，我们就没事了。The majority of the site&#039;s userbase is from the US, so when I see an article that assumes that I&#039;m also in the US, as a UK resident, I immediately feel ostracised. For example, if you say &amp;quot;SCP-XXXX is located in North Carolina&amp;quot; without specifying &amp;quot;North Carolina, US&amp;quot;, you&#039;re expecting that the person accessing this SCP document is in the US, and by extension the Foundation is US-only, and therefore as a UK reader, I don&#039;t count. Make your locations international and we&#039;re good.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;请不要排除任何人，哪怕是无意的。Try not to exclude anyone, even unintentionally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;缺乏视觉描述：Lack of visual description:&lt;/strong&gt;如果你在告诉我某个东西——它可能是一个物体、一个地点，什么都好——&lt;em&gt;求求你&lt;/em&gt;把它详细描述。视觉描述，对我来说，是看文的时候最重要的东西：我个人必须得在脑海里看见它才能恰当地理解它。如果你不描述它，我就会开始假设；而如果你打破了这些假设（一定会这样，因为你不知道我假设了什么），我就会感到疑惑。 if you&#039;re telling me about something - be it an object, an action, a location, or literally anything - &lt;em&gt;please please please&lt;/em&gt; describe it in detail. Visual description is the single most important thing to me when it comes to enjoying your article: I personally have to be able to see it in my mind to understand it properly. If you don&#039;t describe it, I&#039;ll assume things; and when you break those assumptions (which you will, because you don&#039;t know what they are), I get confused.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;很简单但也很容易遗漏——如果你的角色走进了一家咖啡店，我可能会假设收银台在右边，而当你说到你的角色对左边的收银员说话的时候我就会感到疑惑。描述房间的时候，请点出收银台在左边，我们就没事了。It&#039;s simple but easy to miss things - if your character walks into a coffee shop, I may assume that the cashier is on the right, and then get confused when you say your character talks to the cashier on the left. When you describe the room, specify that the cashier is on the left, and we&#039;re good.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not making me feel something:&lt;/strong&gt; there&#039;s a lot of very well-written articles out there that are just dull. You can tell an elegant, beautiful story, but if I don&#039;t come away from that having felt something or having had my opinion changed, the chance of getting an upvote is very slim. If I feel like my time has been wasted reading a series of words rather than a compelling story, there&#039;s a big chance I&#039;ll downvote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A rating module at the end of the article:&lt;/strong&gt; I firmly believe that ratings are meaningless as a measure of quality. So, by sticking another rating module at the end of your article, you&#039;re telling me not only that you disagree, but also that you don&#039;t trust me to remember to vote. If votes are so important to you, maybe you&#039;ll enjoy another.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Losing my interest:&lt;/strong&gt; If I find myself not wanting to continue an article, I am not one of those people who thinks &amp;quot;well, I didn&#039;t read the whole thing, so I have no right to vote.&amp;quot; I will.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;给SCP的指南&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Big headers telling me about a clearance level:&lt;/strong&gt; Clearance levels are &lt;em&gt;very rarely&lt;/em&gt; important to your SCP&#039;s narrative, and when you open with a big image that tells me I need level 4 clearance or whatever, my mindset immediately switches from &amp;quot;open to experiencing an interesting SCP&amp;quot; to pessimist mode. 99.9% of all SCPs have a clearance restriction, why does your SCP&#039;s clearance level need special attention? Use your big header to tell me about &lt;em&gt;literally&lt;/em&gt; anything else - &lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-3211&quot;&gt;something I need to know immediately&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/taboo&quot;&gt;important containment procedures that affect me as a reader&lt;/a&gt;, or use it to &lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-3448&quot;&gt;give context to your narrative&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP is a common object:&lt;/strong&gt; If I could find the item that your SCP is based on in my house, you&#039;re on track for a downvote. If I feel &lt;em&gt;at all&lt;/em&gt; that the origin of your SCP is &amp;quot;what could I make anomalous?&amp;quot; then your downvote is pretty much guaranteed. Equally, if you&#039;re telling me about an anomalous object but you&#039;re not telling about its origin, then that&#039;s a big weight on the downvote scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the flipside, if your SCP is something unusual - like a concept, or a location, or something abstract, then I&#039;m all ears.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The word &amp;quot;will&amp;quot;:&lt;/strong&gt; Compulsion effects for the sake of them are lazy writing. SCP-XXXX will do this, the subject will then do this, then X happens, then the SCP will do this. You&#039;ve already lost my interest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing testing testing:&lt;/strong&gt; the Foundation contains. We&#039;re not Aperture Science - once you&#039;ve done enough tests to establish the most effective way to contain something, &lt;em&gt;stop&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Redaction:&lt;/strong&gt; I explained my opinion better &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-7159089/your-unpopular-scp-opinions#post-3940816&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;, but the gist is don&#039;t redact anything unless you&#039;ve clearly explained (or will clearly explain, later in the article) why it&#039;s being redacted. Redacted names of people and places is meaningless (just pick a name/a random place!), and redaction as a substitute for content (&amp;quot;SCP-XXXX then proceeded to [redacted]&amp;quot;) can be an instant downvote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spooky notes at the end:&lt;/strong&gt; There are &lt;em&gt;so, so many&lt;/em&gt; articles that conclude with &lt;em&gt;oooo a spooky note&lt;/em&gt; or a corrupted-text collapsible or something. Please just fuck off. Come up with something more original.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;给001提案的指南&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;无论如何我都可能会差评它：&lt;/strong&gt;001提案数目的膨胀，尤其是有些做作想写不止一篇，已经贬值了这个曾经对我来说价值非凡的格式。因此，我对001的标准高得不正常，基本上什么都是差评。让我震惊。任何一个我给出去的好评都是无比反复无常的——如果我读完了然后好评了，我可能会在一个月后回来，然后发现我其实没有被惊艳到，我就会取消好评。 Inflation in 001 proposal numbers, especially with some authors making more than one proposal, has cheapened the once-valuable meaning of the format for me. As a result, my standards are so ridiculously high for 001s that a downvote is basically guaranteed. Amaze me. Any upvotes that I do give out are extremely volatile - if I read it and upvote, then I come back a month later and find that I&#039;m not amazed any more, that upvote disappears.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;给搞笑文章的指南&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;对于搞笑文章，其他所有指南都可以无视，只需要重视一件事：&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;它不好笑：&lt;/strong&gt;如果我笑了，我就给好评，没有笑，就差评。就是这样。如果我还想说什么深刻的发言的话，我就会留下评论。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;给中心页的指南&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;没有解释中心页的用途：&lt;/strong&gt;要是我读下来，你的中心页没有很好地让我知道我要写什么来给它做出贡献，你就会得到差评。要不然就是好评。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
